{
  "about": "A post page (appendix A 18-20): the responses a post page needs, each a data object {media: {...}} as Threads returns it, read into the post, its parent chain and its first batch of direct replies with their sub-replies, plus reply coverage. post_id is the id the shortcode encodes (targets.json shortcodes). Roles are told apart by shape, never by query name: the media whose code is the requested shortcode is the post, containing_thread holds the parents, direct_replies holds the replies; each response must be about post_id. A direct reply edge is node.posts.edges[].node, the first being the direct reply and the rest what hangs under it (sub-replies, or the replier continuing). depth comes from reply_to_id; relation is reply (a different author answers) or continuation (the author of the post it answers continues it). limit counts direct replies shown. An object {\"$user\": \"A\"} stands for users.A. All content is synthetic. Every synthetic code is the shortcode of its post's pk (base64url digits, targets.json shortcodes), so a post URL names that same post with no request.",
